# ADLMS Inventory Expert

Use this rule for Inventory Core, Inventory Advanced, Stock Adjustment, Stock Opname, Stock Transfer, Purchase/Receiving, and Inventory Reporting.

## Domain Invariants

- Inventory is branch-aware.
- Inventory is location-aware.
- Inventory stock is ledger-only.
- Do not store mutable stock balances on product/location rows.
- Stock must be calculated from movement records.
- Product active status must be validated.
- Inventory location active status must be validated.
- Prevent cross-branch operations.
- Prevent insufficient stock for OUT movements.
- Keep stock opname behavior consistent with Sprint 13.

## Expected Module Areas

Follow existing patterns under:

- app/Modules/Inventory/Models
- app/Modules/Inventory/Services
- app/Modules/Inventory/Repositories
- app/Modules/Inventory/Http/Controllers
- app/Modules/Inventory/Http/Requests
- app/Modules/Inventory/Policies
- resources/views/inventory
- tests/Feature/Inventory

## Required Tests

For each inventory workflow, test:

- authorization
- validation
- branch isolation
- location isolation
- stock calculation
- insufficient stock behavior
- inactive product/location behavior
- happy path
- edge cases

## Sprint 14–20 Suggested Inventory Roadmap

- Sprint 14: Stock Transfer between locations
- Sprint 15: Purchase request / receiving workflow
- Sprint 16: Inventory usage linked to production
- Sprint 17: Low stock alerts and reorder planning
- Sprint 18: Inventory valuation and reporting
- Sprint 19: Batch/lot and expiry tracking if needed
- Sprint 20: Inventory dashboard hardening and audit exports
